# LeakSanitizer suppressions for Byte-Engine test runs.
#
# Use with: ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1 LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=lsan.supp
#
# A thread that is still running when the process exits owns bookkeeping that Rust's thread startup
# allocates (thread-local destructor registration, the `Thread` handle, its parking semaphore). LSan
# reports it as leaked even though the thread would release it on exit. The frame below is the one every
# such report has in common.
#
# The known sources are threads the engine cannot stop yet:
# - HttpInspectorServer: oxhttp 0.3.3 has no way to stop its listener thread, so dropping the server
#   leaves the thread running.
# - Worker pools (asset manager, EXR decoding) that are still shutting down at process exit.
#
# This also hides a genuinely leaked thread, so drop this entry if a thread's cleanup needs auditing.
leak:6thread7current11set_current
